  "result": "I added `click.KeyValue`, following the approved plan. The full test suite passes: 1915 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed, 0 failed.\n\n`click.KeyValue()` parses `key=value` into a `(key, value)` tuple:\n- It splits on the first `=`, so `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")`, and `a=` gives `(\"a\", \"\")`.\n- Input with no `=` or an empty key fails with `'abc' is not a valid key=value pair.`, which is shown as a usage error with exit code 2.\n- An already-converted tuple, such as a default, passes through unchanged.\n\nChanges:\n- **`src/click/types.py`**: the `KeyValue` class, placed after `UUIDParameterType`.\n- **`src/click/__init__.py`**: the export.\n- **`tests/test_types.py`**: tests for valid inputs, failure cases, and a `multiple=True` option.\n- **`tests/test_info_dict.py`**: an info-dict case.\n- **`docs/api.md`** and **`docs/parameter-types.md`**: documentation entries.\n- **`CHANGES.md`**: a changelog entry under a new \"Unreleased\" heading. I first put it under 8.5.0, which was already released, and corrected that.\n\nI didn't commit anything, since you didn't ask for a commit.",
